    "reason": "The artifact diff [ev-7b1bee6d2352] shows only that the ManagedResourceActivationPolicy v1alpha1 CRD is new in the target release. The proposed exposure, not gvk-in-use for that kind, would match every environment upgrading from a release where the API did not exist yet. So it does not narrow exposure down to anything. The only guidance is \"install or update CRDs before upgrading if you manage them separately.\" None of the evidence names a values key, flag or field that shows whether an environment manages CRDs separately, and it does not say what fails if they don't. So no correct exposure condition follows from the evidence.",
